#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Codex Switch system test: the whole system, on the real path, in about 20 seconds.

Each group of outcomes gets its own isolated system: a private launchd job on a
spare port running a build of this working tree (or, for the first update, the
newest published release or v0.1.9), its own data directory with fake accounts, and fake
providers in place of OpenAI and Anthropic. The groups run at once. The
official Codex, Pi and Claude Code clients drive each system; a scripted model
answers them, so no tokens are spent and no real service is waited on. Prints
what the system did for each outcome and leaves nothing running. Evidence stays
in .project-private/system-test.

scripts/dev/smoke-test checks the real services with real accounts.
"""
